From 1e1393121126f43cd044386738844d1ba6c2458c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 01:34:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08131/11362] [outer-loop] ARC generation ablation: 4
 induce-prompt arms on held-out engine accuracy

240 induce cells (20 games x 4 arms x 3 replicates), gemma-4-31B-it-qat on 2x RTX 3090,
CUDA build proven from /proc/<pid>/exe. Induce on the prefix only; score the withheld
tail plus a large fresh offline-exploration set. No behaviour, no episode, no gate.

TARGET NOT REACHED. 0 engines reach change_accuracy >= 0.5 on substantive held-out rows
with more than a handful of rows. The primary (tail change_accuracy, plain branch) is
effectively floored: 8 of 9 game pairs tie at 0.0 in every contrast.

The one large-n hit is hollow and is the main finding. bp35__r1__antiid scored 0.5662 on
219 clean fresh rows (0 leaks re-verified, 120 distinct correct next_grids) -- and all 124
of its exact matches change EXACTLY ONE CELL. Restricted to rows where reality changed >=2
cells it scores 0.0. It induced the row-63 progress counter and none of the dynamics.
change_accuracy weights a 1-cell HUD tick like a 47-cell state change, so the headline bar
is clearable without modelling anything. Both strata are reported with denominators.

Also measured: the code-only directive does NOT achieve its stated purpose on this
generator (base emits 0.658 comment-line fraction vs think's 0.277 and leaks control
tokens into source in 52/59 engines); anti-identity eliminates identity engines
(11.9% -> 0.0%) and yields zero additional substantive exact matches, so identity was
never the binding constraint; the delta arm backfires (identity 20.8%).

Instrument proven reachable BEFORE the arms: a hand-written oracle hits 1.0 on all 20
tails, identity hits 0.0 everywhere, so every zero here is measured, not forced. Newly
measured ceiling: 8 of 11 hidden-state games show same-grid+same-action -> different
next-grid; 0 of 9 plain games do -- HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS corroborated from data.

Arm delivery witnessed on the wire 240/240; 225 distinct engines, 0 bit-identical
replicates or cross-arm collisions; ledger reconciles 225 scored + 15 missing = 240.
All 225 engine files re-hashed against their emission-time sha256: 0 mismatches.

Not submitted; no scored or online game played. No shipped default flipped.
adversarial_verify + summarize_artifact clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
